{"name":"Sovereign","hex":"#4b4356","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sovereign","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The title of a monarch.","God, the supreme being who has power over all creation."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from German."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sovereign"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sovereign","blocks":[{"text":"Sovereign is a title that can be applied to the highest leader in various categories. The word is borrowed from Old French souverain, which is ultimately derived from the Latin superānus, meaning 'above'."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sovereign"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Queen_Elizabeth_II_official_portrait_for_1959_tour_%28retouched%29_%28cropped%29_%283-to-4_aspect_ratio%29.jpg/500px-Queen_Elizabeth_II_official_portrait_for_1959_tour_%28retouched%29_%28cropped%29_%283-to-4_aspect_ratio%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Queen_Elizabeth_II_official_portrait_for_1959_tour_%28retouched%29_%28cropped%29_%283-to-4_aspect_ratio%29.jpg/500px-Queen_Elizabeth_II_official_portrait_for_1959_tour_%28retouched%29_%28cropped%29_%283-to-4_aspect_ratio%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Queen Elizabeth II was the sovereign of 32 independent realms over the course of her reign, with her role in each realm separate and legally distinct.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQueen_Elizabeth_II_official_portrait_for_1959_tour_(retouched)_(cropped)_(3-to-4_aspect_ratio).jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}